<!-- ═══════════════════════ ABOUT ══════════════════════ -->
<div id="section-about" class="page-section">
  <div style="padding-top:100px;"></div>
  <section>
    <div class="section-inner" style="max-width:760px;">
      <p class="section-label reveal">Our Story</p>
      <h2 class="section-title reveal">The mandate stands.<br><em>Now we build.</em></h2>
      <div class="reveal" style="font-family:var(--font-b);font-size:19px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--text);">
        <p style="margin-bottom:24px;">For eleven years, Rickey Jay Bennett II preached the Word of God on the streets of America. Not from a pulpit. Not with a salary or a congregation or a denominational charter behind her. She preached from sidewalks and shelters and bus stations — with only a Bible and a conviction that would not leave her alone.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:24px;">The conviction was this: that work is sacred. That the capacity for productive, skilled, dignified labor is not a feature of economic life but a feature of human nature — given by a Creator God who worked in the beginning, before sin entered the world.</p>
        <p style="margin-bottom:24px;">The Thessalonian Mandate Institute was not born in a boardroom or a seminary or a nonprofit incubator. It was born in the understanding that the work mandate of 2 Thessalonians 3:10 is not a comfort. It is a command — and a command carries with it a corresponding obligation.</p>
        <p style="font-style:italic;color:var(--gold);">The mandate stands. Now we build.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="fade-rule" style="margin:48px 0;"></div>
      <p class="section-label reveal">The Minister</p>
      <h3 class="reveal" style="font-family:var(--font-d);font-size:28px;font-weight:400;color:var(--text);margin-bottom:20px;">Rickey Jay Bennett II</h3>
      <p class="reveal" style="font-family:var(--font-b);font-size:17px;line-height:1.8;color:var(--text-light);margin-bottom:12px;">Founder · Minister · Chief Executive · Secretary · Treasurer</p>
      <p class="reveal" style="font-family:var(--font-b);font-size:17px;line-height:1.85;color:var(--text);">An independent minister, street preacher, and researcher whose work spans artificial intelligence, philosophy of mind, and the theology of human labor. She founded the Institute on the conviction that the Church is obligated to equip those who are willing to work but cannot — and built it as the thing that should have already existed.</p>
      <div class="fade-rule" style="margin:48px 0;"></div>
      <div class="reveal">
        <p class="section-label">Legal Foundation</p>
        <p style="font-family:var(--font-u);font-size:13px;font-weight:300;color:var(--text-light);line-height:1.8;">The Thessalonian Mandate Institute is a Faith-Based Organization established in Austin, Texas, operating under the automatic tax exemption of 26 U.S.C. § 508(c)(1)(A). EIN issued by the Internal Revenue Service. All operations are subordinate to the theological convictions set forth in the Statement of Faith and Theological Framework.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</div>

